# --- Project outputs ----------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberate policy: the *generated* artifacts are COMMITTED, because a reviewer
# should be able to read the report and see the figures without installing
# anything or running the pipeline.
#
#   COMMITTED:  reports/figures/*.png, reports/artifacts/*.json,
#               reports/project_report.docx, reports/presentation.pptx,
#               models/model.joblib, models/model_card.json,
#               data/processed/cleaned.csv
#   IGNORED:    logs, caches, scratch work
#
# The trained model is committed on purpose. Normally you would keep binaries
# out of git, but the deployed Streamlit app has no build step that could train
# one — if model.joblib is not in the repo, the live demo simply cannot make
# predictions. It is a single file of roughly 1-3 MB for a forest of this size,
# which is well within what git handles comfortably. If it ever grows past
# ~50 MB, move it to Git LFS or a release asset rather than ignoring it.

logs/
*.log

# Scratch space for experiments that should not ship
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
